  "totalVideoDuration": 199.421,
  "slides": [
    {
      "slide": 1,
      "narrationText": "Welcome. This presentation introduces the Pyramid Paradigm for Manufacturing Systems: a configurable framework for industrial AI strategy, architecture and decision support. The purpose is to create a clear shared structure for mapping organisational levels, data, models, agents, connectivity and decisions.",
      "narrationDuration": 19.409,
      "leadSilence": 0.4,
      "trailingSilence": 0.5,
      "slideVideoDuration": 19.867,
      "startTimestamp": 0,
      "endTimestamp": 19.867,
      "sourceImage": "attached_assets/Slide_1_1790088628872.png",
      "renderedImage": "work/pyramid-video/slides-1920x1080/slide_01.png",
      "audioFile": "output/audio/slide_01.wav",
      "segmentFile": "work/pyramid-video/segments/slide_01.mp4"
    },
    {
      "slide": 2,
      "narrationText": "Manufacturing needs this type of framework because industrial manufacturing systems are rarely a single-tool problem. It involves plant-scale complexity, heterogeneous information, multiple time horizons and the need to turn insight into action. Also, different parts of a manufacturing organisation view the same system through very different lenses. Shop-floor teams focus on signals, process conditions and immediate performance, while engineering, management and executive functions interpret information in terms of quality, optimisation, resources, risk and strategy. The Pyramid Paradigm provides a shared structure that connects these different perspectives without losing their organisational context. The pyramid gives organisations a practical starting point.",
      "narrationDuration": 46.086,
      "leadSilence": 0.4,
      "trailingSilence": 0.5,
      "slideVideoDuration": 46.633,
      "startTimestamp": 19.867,
      "endTimestamp": 66.5,
      "sourceImage": "attached_assets/Slide_2_1790088628872.png",
      "renderedImage": "work/pyramid-video/slides-1920x1080/slide_02.png",
      "audioFile": "output/audio/slide_02.wav",
      "segmentFile": "work/pyramid-video/segments/slide_02.mp4"
    },
    {
      "slide": 3,
      "narrationText": "At the heart of the paradigm is one structural frame and five connected viewpoints. The structural frame anchors the organisation, while the data, models, agentic, connectivity and decision-making pyramids each reveal a different but connected layer of industrial intelligence.",
      "narrationDuration": 16.391,
      "leadSilence": 0.4,
      "trailingSilence": 0.5,
      "slideVideoDuration": 16.933,
      "startTimestamp": 66.5,
      "endTimestamp": 83.433,
      "sourceImage": "attached_assets/Slide_3_1790088628871.png",
      "renderedImage": "work/pyramid-video/slides-1920x1080/slide_03.png",
      "audioFile": "output/audio/slide_03.wav",
      "segmentFile": "work/pyramid-video/segments/slide_03.mp4"
    },
    {
      "slide": 4,
      "narrationText": "The structural frame can be adapted to each organisation. Levels, sectors and sub-layers can be renamed or expanded, so a small plant, a large enterprise or a multi-site programme can all use the same logic without forcing a fixed template.",
      "narrationDuration": 14.36,
      "leadSilence": 0.4,
      "trailingSilence": 0.5,
      "slideVideoDuration": 14.867,
      "startTimestamp": 83.433,
      "endTimestamp": 98.3,
      "sourceImage": "attached_assets/Slide_4_1790088628871.png",
      "renderedImage": "work/pyramid-video/slides-1920x1080/slide_04.png",
      "audioFile": "output/audio/slide_04.wav",
      "segmentFile": "work/pyramid-video/segments/slide_04.mp4"
    },
    {
      "slide": 5,
      "narrationText": "The data pyramid organises information into usable assets. Data is mapped by organisational level and by sector, with each data brick capturing source, characteristics, preparation needs and intended purpose. This helps expose what is available and what is missing.",
      "narrationDuration": 16.53,
      "leadSilence": 0.4,
      "trailingSilence": 0.5,
      "slideVideoDuration": 17.033,
      "startTimestamp": 98.3,
      "endTimestamp": 115.333,
      "sourceImage": "attached_assets/Slide_5_1790088628871.png",
      "renderedImage": "work/pyramid-video/slides-1920x1080/slide_05.png",
      "audioFile": "output/audio/slide_05.wav",
      "segmentFile": "work/pyramid-video/segments/slide_05.mp4"
    },
    {
      "slide": 6,
      "narrationText": "The models pyramid shows that manufacturing value comes from combining model families. Physics-based models, statistical methods, vision models, optimisation and AI can coexist. The right model is chosen based on the question, available data and decision context.",
      "narrationDuration": 16.913,
      "leadSilence": 0.4,
      "trailingSilence": 0.5,
      "slideVideoDuration": 17.4,
      "startTimestamp": 115.333,
      "endTimestamp": 132.733,
      "sourceImage": "attached_assets/Slide_6_1790088628871.png",
      "renderedImage": "work/pyramid-video/slides-1920x1080/slide_06.png",
      "audioFile": "output/audio/slide_06.wav",
      "segmentFile": "work/pyramid-video/segments/slide_06.mp4"
    },
    {
      "slide": 7,
      "narrationText": "The agentic and connectivity view shows how selected data and models become purposeful agents. Agents consume defined inputs, apply model logic, produce outputs and trigger actions. Connectivity then routes those outputs to people, systems, assets and decisions.",
      "narrationDuration": 17.122,
      "leadSilence": 0.4,
      "trailingSilence": 0.5,
      "slideVideoDuration": 17.6,
      "startTimestamp": 132.733,
      "endTimestamp": 150.333,
      "sourceImage": "attached_assets/Slide_7_1790088628871.png",
      "renderedImage": "work/pyramid-video/slides-1920x1080/slide_07.png",
      "audioFile": "output/audio/slide_07.wav",
      "segmentFile": "work/pyramid-video/segments/slide_07.mp4"
    },
    {
      "slide": 8,
      "narrationText": "The decision-making pyramid makes clear that intelligence is useful at every level. Data and models support shop-floor decisions, engineering choices, management planning and executive strategy, while maintaining context across the organisation.",
      "narrationDuration": 14.278,
      "leadSilence": 0.4,
      "trailingSilence": 0.5,
      "slideVideoDuration": 14.833,
      "startTimestamp": 150.333,
      "endTimestamp": 165.167,
      "sourceImage": "attached_assets/Slide_8_1790088628870.png",
      "renderedImage": "work/pyramid-video/slides-1920x1080/slide_08.png",
      "audioFile": "output/audio/slide_08.wav",
      "segmentFile": "work/pyramid-video/segments/slide_08.mp4"
    },
    {
      "slide": 9,
      "narrationText": "In practice, an engagement can progress through six steps: define the structure, map the data, align the models, design agents, connect flows and enable decisions. Completed pyramids can become reusable templates for future plants, processes and sectors.",
      "narrationDuration": 15.799,
      "leadSilence": 0.4,
      "trailingSilence": 0.5,
      "slideVideoDuration": 16.367,
      "startTimestamp": 165.167,
      "endTimestamp": 181.533,
      "sourceImage": "attached_assets/Slide_9_1790088628870.png",
      "renderedImage": "work/pyramid-video/slides-1920x1080/slide_09.png",
      "audioFile": "output/audio/slide_09.wav",
      "segmentFile": "work/pyramid-video/segments/slide_09.mp4"
    },
    {
      "slide": 10,
      "narrationText": "The overall impact is clarity, readiness, alignment, actionability and scalability. The Pyramid Paradigm gives customers a premium consultancy lens for understanding where to begin, what capabilities they need and how to organise industrial AI into a coherent manufacturing system.",
      "narrationDuration": 17.355,
      "leadSilence": 0.4,
      "trailingSilence": 0.5,
      "slideVideoDuration": 17.867,
      "startTimestamp": 181.533,
      "endTimestamp": 199.4,
      "sourceImage": "attached_assets/Slide_10_1790088628870.png",
      "renderedImage": "work/pyramid-video/slides-1920x1080/slide_10.png",
      "audioFile": "output/audio/slide_10.wav",
      "segmentFile": "work/pyramid-video/segments/slide_10.mp4"
    }
  ],
